// Command gencrd generates a Krateo widget CRD from a widget JSON schema.
//
// WHY THIS LIVES HERE. Widget CRDs used to be generated by shelling out to `krateoctl
// gen-widget`, installed in CI by piping a release script to bash. That put the definition of
// this repo's own CRDs in another repository, on another release cadence, reachable only through
// a `curl | bash` whose pinned version three workflows had to agree on. The widget schemas are
// here; the CRDs they produce ship from here; the generator belongs here too.
//
// WHAT IT DELIBERATELY DOES NOT DO: reimplement CRD generation. It calls
// krateo-platformops/plumbing/crdgen, the same library core-provider and oasgen-provider use,
// because that library validates its output through the apiserver's OWN
// validation.ValidateCustomResourceDefinition before returning (crdgen/transpile.go). A
// generator that cannot be refused by the apiserver cannot emit a CRD the apiserver would
// reject — and the failure it prevents is silent: an invalid CRD is refused at apply time while
// the previous version keeps serving, so a widget gains a field, the CRD that would admit it is
// refused, and the field is pruned on write with nothing reporting an error. A second
// implementation, in TypeScript or otherwise, cannot have that property; it could only
// approximate it, and its wrongness would be quiet.
//
// So this is a thin front end: read the schema, lift `properties.spec`, graft on the four
// envelope sub-schemas that every widget carries, narrow `resourcesRefs[].resource` to the
// kinds the widget declares, and hand the result to crdgen.
package main
